# `@Flatten` of an expression that is no name, a constant whose value is a dynamic a
# function gave whole (Semantics ch. 7 and Appendix B, `@Flatten`; ruling FV): the outer
# never fires, so the flatten is its one inner and moves as that inner does.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

$Choose: fn Bool, $Nat, $Nat -> $Nat
fn $Choose second, $p, $q = if second: $q else: $p

@main: @unit
@main:
    !go <- Ui.Button($label=$"go")                                # 0
    $a <- 5 then $a + 1 on !go
    $b <- 20 then $b + 2 on !go
    $shown <- @Flatten ($ ($Choose True, $a, $b))
    Ui.Label($text=$"{$shown}")                                   # 1
